#
# Curated proper-noun allow-list for the production English system lexicon.
# One surface form per line; lines starting with '#' are comments.
# The lookup key is the ASCII case-folded form; the surface form here is the
# shipped canonical display. A curated form whose canonical differs from its
# fold only by a leading capital (Apple, Google) never overrides an existing
# SCOWL word — lowercase typing keeps the generic display, and the casing
# the user typed is preserved by the English Core arc rule. Curated forms
# with internal or full uppercase (iPhone, macOS, PDF) always win.
# Maintainers add entries only after review; see data-licenses/english/AUDIT.md §6.
